### macOS
.DS_Store
*.icloud

### Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
*.log
coverage/
.nyc_output/

### Env / secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

### Build artifacts
/dist/
/.tmp/

### Generated site. `site/docs/` is a mirror of `docs/` written by
### site/scripts/sync-docs.ts; `docs/` is the tracked source of truth.
/site/docs/
/site/.vitepress/cache/
/site/.vitepress/dist/

### Decks and documents the example writes
/examples/out/

### Editors
.idea/
*.swp
*~

### Claude Code local/runtime files (shared config like .claude/settings.json stays tracked)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.lock
### `.claude/skills` is a junction on Windows; tools that read it as a symlink
### rather than a directory skip a `skills/` pattern, so match it without the slash.
.claude/skills

### Skills installed from a dependency rather than authored here. `skills-lock.json`
### is the tracked record; `npx skills experimental_install` restores the copy, which
### then always matches the installed package version. A skill this repo writes itself
### is not covered by this and stays tracked.
/.agents/skills/ts-pptx-upstream/
